1
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:10,800
The rousing, rollicking adventure of the world's first rockin' rooster!

2
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:15,600
Rock-A-Doodle is a comedy, family, animation film directed by Don Bluth.

3
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:20,400
Chanticleer is a foolhardy farm rooster who believes his crows
can actually make the sun come up and shine.

4
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:25,200
When the sun rises one morning without Chanticleer's crow, he leaves the farm
in disgrace and runs off to become a rock 'n' roll singer.

5
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:30,000
But in his absence, a sinister, sunshine-hating owl prepares to take over.

6
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:34,800
Chanticleer / The King (voice), played by Glen Campbell.

7
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:39,600
Edmond, played by Toby Scott Ganger.

8
00:24:38,400 --> 00:24:44,400
Grand Duke (voice), played by Christopher Plummer.

9
00:27:43,200 --> 00:27:49,200
Dory - Mother, played by Kathryn Holcomb.

10
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Frank - Dad, played by Stan Ivar.

11
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:58,800
Goldie (voice), played by Ellen Greene.

12
00:36:57,600 --> 00:37:03,600
Rock-a-Doodle is a 1991 independent animated musical comedy film produced by
Sullivan Bluth Studios Ireland Limited and Goldcrest Films.

13
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:08,400
Loosely based on Edmond Rostand's 1910 comedy play Chantecler,
Rock-a-Doodle was directed by Don Bluth and written by David N.

14
00:43:07,200 --> 00:43:13,200
The film features the voices of Christopher Plummer, Phil Harris (in his final film role), Glen Campbell, Sorrell Booke,
Sandy Duncan, Eddie Deezen, Ellen Greene, Charles Nelson Reilly, and Toby Scott Ganger (in his film debut).

15
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
The film tells the story of an anthropomorphic rooster named Chanticleer,
who lives on a farm and crows every morning to raise the sun.

16
00:49:16,800 --> 00:49:22,800
However, he leaves his farm to become a singer in the city after being tricked by the Grand Duke of Owls,
whose kind hates sunshine, into thinking that his crow does not actually raise the sun.

17
00:52:21,600 --> 00:52:27,600
Without Chanticleer, rain continues to pour non-stop,
causing a massive flood all over the country.

18
00:55:26,400 --> 00:55:32,400
The Duke and his henchmen take over in the darkness, and
plan to eat all of the barnyard animals.

19
00:58:31,200 --> 00:58:37,200
Chanticleer's friends from the farm, along with Edmond, a young human boy who was transformed into a kitten by the Duke,
take off on a mission to get Chanticleer to bring back the sun and save the country before it is too late.

20
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
Rock-a-Doodle was released in the United Kingdom on 2 August 1991
and in the United States and Canada on 3 April 1992.

21
01:04:40,800 --> 01:04:46,800
The film received mostly negative reviews and was a box-office
failure, grossing $11 million on a budget of $18 million.

22
01:07:45,600 --> 01:07:51,600
Nevertheless, it would achieve greater success on home video and
obtained popularity among many 1990s children.

23
01:10:50,400 --> 01:10:56,400
The film explores themes of cat, chicken, villain,
rooster, live action and animation.

24
01:13:55,200 --> 01:14:01,200
The tone is lighthearted.
